                "senderName": "NWS Austin/San Antonio TX",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued July 18 at 7:59AM CDT until July 20 at 3:00AM CDT by NWS Austin/San Antonio TX",
                "description": "...Forecast flooding changed from Moderate to Major severity and\nincreased in duration for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nDevils River At Pafford Crossing nr Comstock affecting Val Verde\nCounty.\n\n* WHAT...Major flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Devils River at Pafford Crossing nr Comstock.\n\n* WHEN...From this afternoon to early Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 14.0 feet, (4.3 meters), Major flooding. Life\nthreatening flooding for recreationists above Paffords Crossing to\nAmistad Reservoir. Flow is near 150,000 cfs. Livestock should be\nmoved from areas vulnerable to major flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:15 AM CDT Saturday the stage was 2.4 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 4.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage\nthis afternoon to a crest of 14.6 feet this evening. It will\nthen fall below flood stage tomorrow afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of\n14.5 feet on 10/11/1981.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive\ncars through flooded areas.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight by 200 AM CDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
